(EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT) Tj T*
T*
(This Employment Agreement \("Agreement"\) is entered into on this 1st day of April, 2024, by and between:) Tj T*
(Apex Technologies India Private Limited, a company incorporated under the Companies Act, 2013, having its registered office at Prestige Tech Park, Marathahalli-Sarjapur Outer Ring Road, Bangalore 560103, Karnataka, India \(hereinafter referred to as the "Company" or "Employer", which expression shall include its successors and assigns\);) Tj T*
(AND) Tj T*
(Rahul Sharma, an individual residing at Flat 402, Green Glen Layout, Bellandur, Bangalore 560103 \(hereinafter referred to as the "Employee"\).) Tj T*
T*
(WHEREAS the Company desires to employ the Employee, and the Employee desires to accept employment with the Company, on the terms and conditions set forth herein.) Tj T*
T*
(NOW, THEREFORE, IN CONSIDERATION OF THE MUTUAL COVENANTS CONTAINED HEREIN, THE PARTIES AGREE AS FOLLOWS:) Tj T*
T*
(1. APPOINTMENT AND COMMENCEMENT) Tj T*
(1.1 Position and Duties) Tj T*
(The Employee is appointed to the position of Senior Software Engineer. The Employee will report to the Engineering Director and perform duties customary to this position, along with any other responsibilities reasonably assigned by the Company.) Tj T*
(1.2 Commencement Date) Tj T*
(The Employee's employment shall commence on 15th April, 2024 \("Effective Date"\).) Tj T*
(1.3 Location of Employment) Tj T*
(The primary place of employment shall be Bangalore, Karnataka. The Company reserves the right to transfer or reassign the Employee to any other office or client location within India.) Tj T*
T*
(2. PROBATION PERIOD) Tj T*
(2.1 Duration of Probation) Tj T*
(The Employee shall be on probation for a period of three \(3\) months from the Effective Date. The Company may, at its sole discretion, extend this probation period by written communication.) Tj T*
(2.2 Confirmation) Tj T*
(Upon satisfactory completion of the probation period, the Company shall issue a formal letter confirming the Employee's appointment.) Tj T*
T*
(3. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS) Tj T*
(3.1 Fixed and Variable Remuneration) Tj T*
(The Employee shall receive an annual Cost to Company \(CTC\) as detailed in Schedule A attached hereto. All payments are subject to standard statutory deductions including Provident Fund, Professional Tax, and Income Tax deducted at source \(TDS\).) Tj T*
(3.2 Annual Discretionary Bonus) Tj T*
(The Employee may be eligible for a performance bonus as determined by the Company's annual performance review cycle. Any variable compensation or bonus is entirely discretionary and shall be forfeited if the Employee has tendered resignation or is serving a notice period on the date of disbursement.) Tj T*
T*
(4. WORKING HOURS AND LEAVE) Tj T*
(4.1 Business Hours) Tj T*
(Standard working hours are 9:30 AM to 6:30 PM, Monday through Friday. Due to business requirements and client engagements, the Employee may be required to work additional hours without additional compensation.) Tj T*
(4.2 Annual Leave Entitlement) Tj T*
(The Employee shall be entitled to eighteen \(18\) days of earned leave, twelve \(12\) days of casual/sick leave, and national holidays as declared by the Company annually. Unused casual leave cannot be encashed or carried forward.) Tj T*
T*
(CONFIDENTIALITY AND NON-DISCLOSURE) Tj T*
(5.1 Proprietary Information) Tj T*
(During employment and for a period of three \(3\) years following termination of employment for any reason, the Employee shall maintain strict confidentiality regarding all proprietary information, trade secrets, algorithms, customer lists, financial data, and technical processes of the Company.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
