stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 740 Td 13 TL
(5.2 Return of Company Property) Tj T*
(Upon resignation or termination, the Employee shall immediately return all Company property, including laptops, mobile devices, security badges, and all physical or digital files.) Tj T*
T*
(6. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS) Tj T*
(6.1 Work for Hire and Assignment) Tj T*
(All inventions, designs, source code, documentation, trademarks, and literary works created by the Employee during the term of employment, whether on Company premises or using personal equipment, shall be deemed a "work made for hire" under the Copyright Act, 1957.) Tj T*
(6.2 Moral Rights Waiver) Tj T*
(To the maximum extent permissible under applicable law, the Employee irrevocably waives all moral rights in any intellectual property created during the employment term.) Tj T*
T*
(RESTRICTIVE COVENANTS) Tj T*
(7.1 Non-Compete Restriction) Tj T*
(For a period of twelve \(12\) months following the termination of employment, the Employee shall not directly or indirectly accept employment with, consult for, or establish any business competing with the products or services offered by the Company within the territory of India.) Tj T*
(7.2 Non-Solicitation of Clients and Employees) Tj T*
(For a period of twenty-four \(24\) months following termination, the Employee shall not solicit, induce, or attempt to hire any employee of the Company, nor solicit business from any client or prospective customer with whom the Employee had contact in the prior twelve months.) Tj T*
T*
(8. TERMINATION AND NOTICE PERIOD) Tj T*
(8.1 Notice Period) Tj T*
(Either party may terminate this employment agreement by providing sixty \(60\) days prior written notice.) Tj T*
(8.2 Payment in Lieu of Notice) Tj T*
(The Company reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to waive the notice period by paying basic salary in lieu of notice. The Employee shall not have an automatic right to buy out the notice period unless expressly approved in writing by HR management.) Tj T*
(8.3 Immediate Termination for Cause) Tj T*
(The Company may terminate this Agreement immediately without notice, salary in lieu of notice, or any severance payment, in the event of gross misconduct, material breach of policy, fraud, conviction of a criminal offense, or habitual absence.) Tj T*
T*
(9. SERVICE BOND AND LIQUIDATED DAMAGES) Tj T*
(9.1 Minimum Service Period) Tj T*
(In consideration of specialized training provided by the Company upon joining, the Employee agrees to serve the Company for a minimum commitment period of twenty-four \(24\) months from the Effective Date.) Tj T*
(9.2 Recovery Amount) Tj T*
(If the Employee resigns or terminates employment prior to completing twenty-four months, the Employee shall immediately pay the Company a sum of INR 2,50,000 \(Rupees Two Lakh Fifty Thousand\) as liquidated damages for training expenses.) Tj T*
T*
(10. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION) Tj T*
(10.1 Governing Law) Tj T*
(This Agreement shall be construed, interpreted, and governed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of India.) Tj T*
(10.2 Jurisdiction and Arbitration) Tj T*
(Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be referred to arbitration in Bangalore, Karnataka, conducted in accordance with the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996. The courts in Bangalore shall have exclusive jurisdiction.) Tj T*
T*
(SCHEDULE A  COMPENSATION) Tj T*
(1. Base Salary: INR 12,00,000 per annum payable in monthly instalments.) Tj T*
(2. House Rent Allowance \(HRA\): INR 6,00,000 per annum.) Tj T*
(3. Special Allowance: INR 4,00,000 per annum.) Tj T*
(4. Annual Performance Variable: Up to INR 3,00,000 per annum based on performance milestones.) Tj T*
ET
